<h1>Visio Nova Mundi CIC</h1><p>Partnership brief · 6 September 2026</p>
<p>A London-based social innovation organisation developing research, community programmes and practical approaches to improving services.</p>
<h2>Ways to collaborate</h2><ul><li>Research and evaluation: needs, service processes and recommendations.</li><li>Pilot design: feasibility, partner responsibilities and readiness.</li><li>Impact measurement: outcome frameworks and evidence plans.</li><li>Advisory and capacity building: workshops, action plans and implementation support.</li></ul>
<h2>Current programme position</h2><p>Unity House Centres is under development. A separate East London community-engagement activity is being prepared. No centre or food-surplus service is operating. Circular Justice remains a discovery-stage concept.</p>
<h2>What helps an initial discussion</h2><p>Describe your organisation or community, the challenge, the support you need, existing evidence and any timing constraints. Scope, responsibilities, costs and delivery dates are agreed before an engagement begins.</p>
<h2>Accountability</h2><p>Company number 16947678. <a href="https://find-and-update.company-information.service.gov.uk/company/16947678">Official company record</a>. Independent ventures featured in Tree of Life retain separate ownership and responsibilities.</p>
<h2>Contact</h2><p><a href="mailto:visionovamundi@outlook.com">visionovamundi@outlook.com</a>. Please send a brief written enquiry without confidential or sensitive data.</p>
